RD! This is what the LORD says: ‘About this time tomorrow at the gate of Samaria, a seah of fine flour will sell for a shekel, and two seahs of barley will sell for a shekel.’”","verse":1},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"But the officer on whose arm the king leaned answered the man of God, “Look, even if the LORD were to make windows in heaven, could this really happen?” “You will see it with your own eyes,” replied Elisha, “but you will not eat any of it.”","verse":2},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"Then the people went out and plundered the camp of the Arameans. It was then that a seah of fine flour sold for a shekel, and two seahs of barley sold for a shekel, according to the word of the LORD.","verse":16},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"And the officer had answered the man of God, “Look, even if the LORD were to make windows in heaven, could this really happen?” So Elisha had replied, “You will see it with your own eyes, but you will not eat any of it!”","verse":19}],"id":"Lord","label":"LORD","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","scope":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","senseReview":"Only literal uppercase LORD is admitted globally. Source Lord article explicitly covers God as Lord; lowercase human lord and sentence-title Lord are not inferred from this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord","term":"LORD"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Lord","sourceTitle":"Lord"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Samaria","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","originalCitations":[{"anchorIndex":2,"href":"?bref=2Kgs.6.24-7.20","rawReference":"2Kgs.6.24-7.20"}],"ruleId":"Samaria::Samaria::reviewed_unambiguous_name","sourceHeadwordId":"Samaria"},"text":"Then Elisha said, “Hear the word of the LORD! This is what the LORD says: ‘About this time tomorrow at the gate of Samaria, a seah of fine flour will sell for a shekel, and two seahs of barley will sell for a shekel.’”","verse":1},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Samaria","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","originalCitations":[{"anchorIndex":2,"href":"?bref=2Kgs.6.24-7.20","rawReference":"2Kgs.6.24-7.20"}],"ruleId":"Samaria::Samaria::reviewed_unambiguous_name","sourceHeadwordId":"Samaria"},"text":"It happened just as the man of God had told the king: “About this time tomorrow at the gate of Samaria, two seahs of barley will sell for a shekel, and a seah of fine flour will sell for a shekel.”","verse":18}],"id":"Samaria","label":"Samaria","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Samaria::Samaria::reviewed_unambiguous_name","scope":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","senseReview":"Reviewed complete original name headword and source subject. Article covers the biblical person(s), named place, or named spiritual figure denoted by this exact spelling; multiple persons under one unchanged source article remain together. Actual proper-name capitalization and whole-name boundaries required. Explicit occurrence-level ambiguity exclusions override this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Samaria","term":"Samaria"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Samaria","sourceTitle":"Samaria"}],"format":"bsb-study-chapter-v2","notes":[{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":["Elisha"],"sourceClass":"profile-title","t":"h"},{"c":["Elisha the prophet was Elijah’s follower and successor in the northern kingdom of Israel during the late 800s ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},", a time when the leaders and people of the northern kingdom turned their backs on God and worshiped the Canaanite god Baal. Ahab and Jezebel were eager worshipers of this false god, as were their descendants who succeeded them on the throne. Elisha’s ministry (853–798 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},") began as King Ahab’s reign was ending; he was an important part of God’s strategy to bring down Israel’s idol-worshiping leaders."],"sourceClass":"profile-body-fl","t":"p"},{"c":["Elisha started his work as a disciple of Elijah and was the one God chose to take Elijah’s place (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.19.15-21","r":"1Kgs.19.15-21","rawR":"1Kgs.19.15-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.19.15-21","value":"1Kgs.19.15-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 19:15-21"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.2.1-18","r":"2Kgs.2.1-18","rawR":"2Kgs.2.1-18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.2.1-18","value":"2Kgs.2.1-18"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 2:1-18"},"). After Elijah was taken into heaven, Elisha’s miracles demonstrated that God’s great power was with him."],"sourceClass":"profile-body","t":"p"},{"c":["Elisha’s miracles often involved water. He purified the putrid water of a spring near Jericho (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.2.19-22","r":"2Kgs.2.19-22","rawR":"2Kgs.2.19-22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.2.19-22","value":"2Kgs.2.19-22"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 2:19-22"},") and caused an ax head to float (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.6.1-7","r":"2Kgs.6.1-7","rawR":"2Kgs.6.1-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.6.1-7","value":"2Kgs.6.1-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 6:1-7"},"). When King Joram’s water supply ran out in enemy territory, Elisha correctly predicted that an ample water supply would emerge (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.3.4-20","r":"2Kgs.3.4-20","rawR":"2Kgs.3.4-20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.3.4-20","value":"2Kgs.3.4-20"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 3:4-20"},"). Baal supposedly controlled water, so these signs showed that the Lord, and not Baal, was really in charge."],"sourceClass":"profile-body","t":"p"},{"c":["Elisha displayed God’s power by helping people in tangible ways. He helped a poor woman by miraculously causing her jars to fill with olive oil (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.4.1-7","r":"2Kgs.4.1-7","rawR":"2Kgs.4.1-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.4.1-7","value":"2Kgs.4.1-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 4:1-7"},"). He predicted to a woman from Shunem that she would have a son, and he brought the boy back to life when he died (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.4.8-37","r":"2Kgs.4.8-37","rawR":"2Kgs.4.8-37","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.4.8-37","value":"2Kgs.4.8-37"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 4:8-37"},"). He cured an Aramean general named Naaman of leprosy (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.5.1-19","r":"2Kgs.5.1-19","rawR":"2Kgs.5.1-19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.5.1-19","value":"2Kgs.5.1-19"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 5:1-19"},"). And he provided food for people who needed it (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.4.38-44","r":"2Kgs.4.38-44","rawR":"2Kgs.4.38-44","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.4.38-44","value":"2Kgs.4.38-44"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 4:38-44"},")."],"sourceClass":"profile-body","t":"p"},{"c":["Elisha was part of God’s plan to bring judgment on the northern kingdom. He anointed both Jehu of Israel and Hazael of Aram (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.8.7-15","r":"2Kgs.8.7-15","rawR":"2Kgs.8.7-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.8.7-15","value":"2Kgs.8.7-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 8:7-15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.9.1-13","r":"2Kgs.9.1-13","rawR":"2Kgs.9.1-13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.9.1-13","value":"2Kgs.9.1-13"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:1-13"},"), who brought a violent end to the leaders of Israel who encouraged the worship of Baal (see ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.19.15-18","r":"1Kgs.19.15-18","rawR":"1Kgs.19.15-18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.19.15-18","value":"1Kgs.19.15-18"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 19:15-18"},")."],"sourceClass":"profile-body","t":"p"},{"c":["Elisha’s miracles anticipated Jesus’ ministry. Jesus also cured lepers (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.8.1-4","r":"Matt.8.1-4","rawR":"Matt.8.1-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.8.1-4","value":"Matt.8.1-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Matt 8:1-4"},"), raised the dead (",{"href":"?bref=Mark.5.21-43","r":"Mark.5.21-43","rawR":"Mark.5.21-43","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.5.21-43","value":"Mark.5.21-43"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mark 5:21-43"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.7.11-17","r":"Luke.7.11-17","rawR":"Luke.7.11-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.7.11-17","value":"Luke.7.11-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Luke 7:11-17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.11.1-44","r":"John.11.1-44","rawR":"John.11.1-44","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.11.1-44","value":"John.11.1-44"}],"t":"ref","v":"John 11:1-44"},"), and miraculously provided food (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.14.13-21","r":"Matt.14.13-21","rawR":"Matt.14.13-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.14.13-21","value":"Matt.14.13-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Matt 14:13-21"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.15.32-38","r":"Matt.15.32-38","rawR":"Matt.15.32-38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.15.32-38","value":"Matt.15.32-38"}],"t":"ref","v":"15:32-38"},"). Jesus mentioned the healing of Naaman as a precedent for his reaching out to Gentiles, to show that God’s mercy is not restricted to Israelites (",{"href":"?bref=Luke.4.27","r":"Luke.4.27","rawR":"Luke.4.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.4.27","value":"Luke.4.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"Luke 4:27"},")."],"sourceClass":"profile-body","t":"p"},{"c":["Passages for Further Study"],"sourceClass":"profile-refs-title","t":"h"},{"c":[{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.19.15-21","r":"1Kgs.19.15-21","rawR":"1Kgs.19.15-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.19.15-21","value":"1Kgs.19.15-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 19:15-21"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.2.1-9.13","r":"2Kgs.2.1-9.13","rawR":"2Kgs.2.1-9.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.2.1-9.13","value":"2Kgs.2.1-9.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 2:1–9:13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.13.14-21","r":"2Kgs.13.14-21","rawR":"2Kgs.13.14-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.13.14-21","value":"2Kgs.13.14-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"13:14-21"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.4.27","r":"Luke.4.27","rawR":"Luke.4.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.4.27","value":"Luke.4.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"Luke 4:27"}],"sourceClass":"profile-refs","t":"p"}],"id":"Profile:Elisha","refs":[{"book":"2KI","endChapter":9,"endVerse":3,"startChapter":2,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Elisha","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"Profile"},"sourceBookAppCode":"2KI","sourceChapterCoverage":[2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"2d542e863a084240d4425468745077e7f12101274d996c05b96f3d510fdbf0ee","sourceItemName":"Elisha","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/Profiles.xml","sourceOrder":54,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"2KI","canonicalOSIS":"2Kgs","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"2Kgs"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"2Kgs.2.1-9.3","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":"Elisha","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Elisha","type":"Profile"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.7.1","r":"2Kgs.7.1","rawR":"2Kgs.7.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.7.1","value":"2Kgs.7.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:1"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["This is what the"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["Lord"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt-divine-name","t":"span"},{"c":[" says:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," Despite Joram’s pessimism and hostility, Elisha brought a message of hope. ",{"c":["Tomorrow"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," would bring a complete change in conditions, with good products again available. • ",{"c":["twelve quarts . . . only one piece of silver:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," Cp. with the prices in ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.6.25","r":"2Kgs.6.25","rawR":"2Kgs.6.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.6.25","value":"2Kgs.6.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"6:25"},"."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:IIKgs.7.1","refs":[{"book":"2KI","endChapter":7,"endVerse":1,"startChapter":7,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"IIKgs.7.1","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"2KI","sourceChapterCoverage":[7],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"8c873f2e5053f9e28c7fe4770d3e2310d92ca1989cf3eaadbec9f6f4e17fcc89","sourceItemName":"IIKgs.7.1","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":4449,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"2KI","canonicalOSIS":"2Kgs","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"2Kgs"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"2Kgs.7.1","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"IIKgs.7.1","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.7.2","r":"2Kgs.7.2","rawR":"2Kgs.7.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.7.2","value":"2Kgs.7.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:2"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The disbelief of Joram’s ",{"c":["officer"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," would cause him to miss God’s blessings."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:IIKgs.7.2","refs":[{"book":"2KI","endChapter":7,"endVerse":2,"startChapter":7,"startVerse":2}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"IIKgs.7.2","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"2KI","sourceChapterCoverage":[7],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"2e514b3154a6ee67a09b246f8dd7ae91f458be933cad7f81e850e22b560a56fe","sourceItemName":"IIKgs.7.2","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":4450,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"2KI","canonicalOSIS":"2Kgs","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"2Kgs"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"2Kgs.7.2","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"IIKgs.7.2","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.7.3","r":"2Kgs.7.3","rawR":"2Kgs.7.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.7.3","value":"2Kgs.7.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:3"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," These ",{"c":["four men"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," were outcasts because of their condition and remained outside ",{"c":["the city gates"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," (",{"href":"?bref=Lev.13.45-46","r":"Lev.13.45-46","rawR":"Lev.13.45-46","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.13.45-46","value":"Lev.13.45-46"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lev 13:45-46"},"; see ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.17.11-13","r":"Luke.17.11-13","rawR":"Luke.17.11-13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.17.11-13","value":"Luke.17.11-13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Luke 17:11-13"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:IIKgs.7.3","refs":[{"book":"2KI","endChapter":7,"endVerse":3,"startChapter":7,"startVerse":3}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"IIKgs.7.3","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"2KI","sourceChapterCoverage":[7],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"008bf90ba27e8f1843f5db4c72e0b7ac94c571ebd304e61646b2375fb447a2b8","sourceItemName":"IIKgs.7.3","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":4451,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"2KI","canonicalOSIS":"2Kgs","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"2Kgs"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"2Kgs.7.3","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"IIKgs.7.3","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.7.5-7","r":"2Kgs.7.5-7","rawR":"2Kgs.7.5-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.7.5-7","value":"2Kgs.7.5-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:5-7"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["The Hittites"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," had settled in the areas just north of Aram and were often in conflict with the Arameans."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:IIKgs.7.5-7","refs":[{"book":"2KI","endChapter":7,"endVerse":7,"startChapter":7,"startVerse":5}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"IIKgs.7.5-7","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"2KI","sourceChapterCoverage":[7],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"63f9c67853f34f2bdcb0639420ec2153c3faad684a0efc81415b00651d3b3382","sourceItemName":"IIKgs.7.5-7","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":4452,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"2KI","canonicalOSIS":"2Kgs","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"2Kgs"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"2Kgs.7.5-7","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"IIKgs.7.5-7","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.7.8-9","r":"2Kgs.7.8-9","rawR":"2Kgs.7.8-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.7.8-9","value":"2Kgs.7.8-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:8-9"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The men realized that they needed to share their good fortune with the people in Samaria."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:IIKgs.7.8-9","refs":[{"book":"2KI","endChapter":7,"endVerse":9,"startChapter":7,"startVerse":8}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"IIKgs.7.8-9","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"2KI","sourceChapterCoverage":[7],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"d0fcb35704b2d58f0a47389773bcd7a6dfe900c999897126e622f3de186e6868","sourceItemName":"IIKgs.7.8-9","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":4453,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"2KI","canonicalOSIS":"2Kgs","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"2Kgs"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"2Kgs.7.8-9","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"IIKgs.7.8-9","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.7.10-12","r":"2Kgs.7.10-12","rawR":"2Kgs.7.10-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.7.10-12","value":"2Kgs.7.10-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:10-12"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," Joram suspected that the Arameans had set a trap, perhaps attempting to lure the Israelites into an ambush. Joshua had used a similar battle tactic in taking the city of Ai (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.8.3-23","r":"Josh.8.3-23","rawR":"Josh.8.3-23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.8.3-23","value":"Josh.8.3-23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Josh 8:3-23"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:IIKgs.7.10-12","refs":[{"book":"2KI","endChapter":7,"endVerse":12,"startChapter":7,"startVerse":10}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"IIKgs.7.10-12","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"2KI","sourceChapterCoverage":[7],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"89ce7c8fb0a998b9cd2119b01300f2d83394171fa00dab9a614351a9354b0b47","sourceItemName":"IIKgs.7.10-12","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":4454,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"2KI","canonicalOSIS":"2Kgs","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"2Kgs"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"2Kgs.7.10-12","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"IIKgs.7.10-12","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.7.13-17","r":"2Kgs.7.13-17","rawR":"2Kgs.7.13-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.7.13-17","value":"2Kgs.7.13-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:13-17"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The trail of abandoned articles confirmed the Arameans’ ",{"c":["rush to escape"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},", and the Israelites ",{"c":["plundered the Aramean camp"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},". True to Elisha’s prophecy, food supplies were now readily available, and Joram’s doubting ",{"c":["officer"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," was ",{"c":["knocked down and trampled to death"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},"."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:IIKgs.7.13-17","refs":[{"book":"2KI","endChapter":7,"endVerse":17,"startChapter":7,"startVerse":13}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"IIKgs.7.13-17","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"2KI","sourceChapterCoverage":[7],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"2f03f120aeca0c295e045d64d07944bfc07de869f5d6dd9979a53b4b2d9efe24","sourceItemName":"IIKgs.7.13-17","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":4455,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"2KI","canonicalOSIS":"2Kgs","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"2Kgs"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"2Kgs.7.13-17","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"IIKgs.7.13-17","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.7.18-20","r":"2Kgs.7.18-20","rawR":"2Kgs.7.18-20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.7.18-20","value":"2Kgs.7.18-20"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:18-20"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The repetition of Elisha’s previous conversation with Joram’s ",{"c":["officer"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," emphasizes the exact fulfillment of the prophecy."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:IIKgs.7.18-20","refs":[{"book":"2KI","endChapter":7,"endVerse":20,"startChapter":7,"startVerse":18}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"IIKgs.7.18-20","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"S